That matches what the task asked for.

• Intent: the new providers::openrouter_routed_preset asks yoagent first. If yoagent rejects a dashed anthropic/ id, it retries with the dotted spelling. So a dashed id works only when its dotted twin does. There's no hand-typed list of versions and no hand-typed limits. Ids with a :variant such as :batch are never rewritten, and other vendors' ids are left alone.
• Where the fix lives: it's in the OpenRouter branch of agent_builder.rs, not in openrouter_anthropic_preset_id as the task said, so that file is outside the task's file list. The commit explains why: yoyo's own Anthropic table has no row for these models and shouldn't grow one. It's a one-line change.
• Tests: expected limits are read from yoagent, not typed in. The near-miss ids (Sonnet 4.5, Opus 4.1, :batch) are covered and still fall back to the guess. A cost test checks that /cost prices the dashed and dotted ids the same as the Anthropic id.
• Consumers and pointers: the new function is used in agent_builder.rs and in the tests. The only #1117 reference left in src, docs and skills is the new doc comment, so no "tracked in #1117" pointers remain.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md is updated to match.
